  required: [date, label, isToday, sessionCount]\n      properties:\n        date: {type: string, format: date}\n        label: {type: string}\n        isToday: {type: boolean}\n        sessionCount: {type: integer}\n    CalendarWeek:\n      type: object\n      required: [weekStart, label, days]\n      properties:\n        weekStart: {type: string, format: date}\n        label: {type: string}\n        days:\n          type: array\n          items: {$ref: '#/components/schemas/CalendarDay'}\n    ScheduleCalendar:\n      type: object\n      required: [today, timezone, weeks]\n      properties:\n        today: {type: string, format: date}\n        timezone: {type: string}\n        weeks:\n          type: array\n          items: {$ref: '#/components/schemas/CalendarWeek'}\n    Error:\n      type: object\n      required: [code, message]\n      properties:\n        code:\n          type: string\n          enum: [already_booked, class_full, not_full, outside_booking_window, class_started, cancelled_by_studio, overlap, booking_limit, invalid_booking_state, not_found, storage_failure, bad_request]\n        message:\n          type: string\n          description: Plain-language message safe to show to the member\n","path":"contracts/openapi.yaml","reason":"The single API contract that the web app's generated client (lib/api) and the local transport both follow."}],"tasks":[{"approach":"Todo: install the packages and build the app once. The scaffold compiles as written. Run the package install and `next build`, and fix only what stops the generated scaffold from compiling, inside these three files. Check that globals.css has the light and dark token sets (prefers-color-scheme), the five type accents, tabular-nums for time and number classes, and a prefers-reduced-motion block that sets transition and animation durations to 0. Do not restyle anything.","conventions":["Keep the factory-generated tokens (CSS variables) as the single source of colours, type, corners and spacing; do not hard-code colours elsewhere","Do not add npm packages"],"dependsOn":[],"exemplars":["app/globals.css","app/layout.tsx"],"fileScope":["app/layout.tsx","package.json","app/globals.css"],"id":"TASK-1","plannedLoc":20,"reqs":["REQ-51","REQ-52","REQ-53","REQ-54","REQ-59"],"title":"Design system: install, build the scaffold, tokens in place"},{"approach":"Implement the stubs.\n- time.ts: londonDate(instant) gives YYYY-MM-DD in London (AC-2.1). formatTime gives HH:mm in London (AC-2.2). formatTimeRange gives 'HH:mm–HH:mm'. dayChipLabel gives 'Mon 12'. dayGroupLabel gives 'Today', 'Tomorrow' or 'Thu 15 Oct'. weekdayShort gives 'Mon'. weekStart gives the Monday. addDays. londonWallTimeToUtc converts a London wall-clock time to a UTC ISO string correctly across DST: guess the offset, then correct it. timeOfDay: Morning <12:00, Afternoon 12:00–16:59, Evening ≥17:00.\n- labels.ts: availabilityLabel per REQ-32 ('Cancelled', 'Full · N on waitlist', '1 spot left', 'Only N left', 'N spots left') and capacityLabel 'N of M spots left'.\n- filters.ts: filterSessions sorts by startsAt, ORs within a group and ANDs across groups, keeps studio-cancelled sessions, and treats an empty group as 'match all'.\n- seed.ts: generateSeed(now). Five instructors (Maya Okafor, Lena Fischer, Jordan Blake, Priya Nair, Marcus Cole), each with a bio and avatarUrl. Use a deterministic generator (seeded by the week-start date) to make ≥20 sessions per week for the current and next London week: all 5 types and 3 rooms, durations from {30,45,60,75}, a 2–4 sentence description, a non-empty whatToBring list. Each week has ≥2 full sessions, ≥2 with 1–3 spots left and ≥1 'Cancelled by studio'. Alex's records: 2 Booked on future, non-overlapping, bookable Scheduled sessions (counted in bookedCount); 1 Waitlisted on a full future session with position ≤ waitlistCount; 3 Attended on sessions that ended before now (create extra past sessions, dated earlier if needed, not shown on Schedule). Nothing on studio-cancelled sessions. generateWeekSessions(weekStart, firstId) is reused for roll-forward (REQ-62) and adds no bookings.\n- storage.ts: KeyValueStorage, createMemoryStorage, loadState (returns null when the key is missing; throws BookingError('storage_failure') when getItem throws; returns null on JSON or version mismatch so the service re-seeds), saveState (throws storage_failure on a setItem error).","conventions":["Pure functions with no React or DOM imports; every time calculation takes an explicit Date or ISO string (no hidden Date.now)","All calendar/day/time-of-day logic uses Intl.DateTimeFormat with timeZone 'Europe/London' and hourCycle h23; store instants as UTC ISO strings","Rule thresholds come only from lib/booking/config.ts","Keep the stub signatures exactly; tests are written against them"],"dependsOn":["TASK-1"],"exemplars":["lib/utils.ts"],"fileScope":["lib/booking/types.ts","lib/booking/errors.ts","lib/booking/config.ts","lib/booking/time.ts","lib/booking/labels.ts","lib/booking/filters.ts","lib/booking/seed.ts","lib/booking/storage.ts"],"id":"TASK-2","plannedLoc":480,"reqs":["REQ-2","REQ-3","REQ-4","REQ-32","REQ-34","REQ-62","REQ-56"],"title":"Booking domain foundations: types, config, London time, labels, filters, seed, storage"},{"approach":"service.ts, createBookingService({storage, clock, seed}):\n- Load state. If none, use seed (a SeedData object or a fn of now; default generateSeed) and save. If the current or next London week has no sessions, add them with generateWeekSessions and save. Never change existing sessions or bookings.\n- book: the check order is in the ADR. Windows (in minutes to start): >10080 or <15 gives outside_booking_window; exactly 10080 or 15 is bookable; start ≤ now gives class_started. Overlap is a strict inequality (touching end-to-start is allowed), message \"You're already booked for <name> at <HH:mm>–<HH:mm>.\". The limit counts Booked records on sessions that have not started (≥10 rejects). Success creates a Booked record and does bookedCount+1.\n- joinWaitlist: same window/start/studio/already checks; not_full if spots remain; position = waitlistCount+1; no overlap or limit check.\n- cancel: status must be Booked (else invalid_booking_state), then started. late = minutesToStart < 120. If waitlistCount > 0 then waitlistCount-1, else bookedCount-1. Clear skipReason.\n- leaveWaitlist: status must be Waitlisted, then started. Set Cancelled with late=false, waitlistCount-1, and move every Waitlisted position behind it up by one.\n- undoBooking: the record must be Booked and created ≤ UNDO_WINDOW_MS ago. Delete the record and do bookedCount-1.\n- simulateOtherMemberCancellation per REQ-21/22: if Alex is #1 and eligible, set Booked, null position, waitlist-1, and push a PromotionNotice. If ineligible, store skipReason {code, message} and either waitlist-1 (others waiting) or booked-1 (Alex alone). If Alex is at #>1, position-1 and waitlist-1. If no waitlist, booked-1.\n- Derived reads (rules.ts/views.ts): a Booked record whose session has ended reads as Attended. A Booked or Waitlisted record on a studio-cancelled session reads as 'Cancelled by studio' and goes in Past. A Waitlisted record whose session has ended is hidden.\n- getMyBookings: upcoming = Booked/Waitlisted on sessions not yet ended, sorted ascending, grouped Today/Tomorrow/'Thu 15 Oct'. Past = Attended, Cancelled and Cancelled by studio, newest first.\n- getStats per REQ-30, with streak weeks Monday–Sunday in London. getActionState uses the precedence in the ADR, with reason texts 'Class has started', 'Cancelled by studio', 'Booking opens 7 days before class', 'Booking closes 15 minutes before class'.\n- consumePromotionNotices returns the stored notices and clears them.\n\nlocal-fetch.ts: createLocalFetch(getService) parses method and path from the Request/URL under LOCAL_API_BASE_URL and dispatches each contract operation to the service. Map errors: not_found→404, bad query→400, storage_failure→500, other rule codes→409. Return JSON Response objects shaped like the contract (views.ts builds SessionSummary/SessionDetail/Booking DTOs incl. availabilityLabel, capacityLabel, actionState.label, badge, lateIfCancelledNow).\n\nsetup.ts: configureLocalApi() builds a singleton service over window.localStorage with systemClock, then sets the generated lib/api client's baseUrl to LOCAL_API_BASE_URL and its fetch to the local fetch. It is idempotent and safe to call from every container.\n\nuse-promotion-notices.ts: a hook that calls consumePromotionNotices once per app session (module flag) and shows an info toast \"Good news! You're off the waitlist and booked for <name> · <Ddd HH:mm>\".","conventions":["Every mutation is synchronous: validate, build the next state, saveState, then commit to memory; if saving fails, keep the old state and return {ok:false, error: storage_failure}","Errors are returned as BookingOutcome {ok:false, error: BookingError} with a plain-language message, never thrown to the UI","The local fetch must never call the global fetch (NFR-12)","Response bodies match contracts/openapi.yaml schemas exactly"],"dependsOn":["TASK-2"],"exemplars":["lib/booking/filters.ts","lib/utils.ts"],"fileScope":["lib/booking/service.ts","lib/booking/rules.ts","lib/booking/views.ts","lib/api-local/local-fetch.ts","lib/api-local/setup.ts","lib/hooks/use-promotion-notices.ts"],"id":"TASK-3","plannedLoc":700,"reqs":["REQ-4","REQ-5","REQ-6","REQ-7","REQ-8","REQ-9","REQ-10","REQ-11","REQ-13","REQ-14","REQ-15","REQ-16","REQ-17","REQ-18","REQ-19","REQ-21","REQ-22","REQ-24","REQ-25","REQ-26","REQ-27","REQ-28","REQ-30","REQ-31","REQ-60","REQ-62","REQ-63","NFR-7","NFR-12"],"title":"Booking service (all rules) and the local API transport for the generated client"},{"approach":"Load: the container takes sessionId (route param, or a prop when embedded as the Schedule side panel) and calls getSession. Show the loading skeleton while it runs. A 404 or 500 shows the error state using the approved copy, with Retry and Back.\n\nFooter, from actionState:\n- book: 'Book this class' plus availability.\n- join_waitlist: \"You'd be #N\".\n- booked: destructive 'Cancel booking' plus \"You're booked\".\n- waitlisted: 'Leave waitlist' plus \"You're #N on the waitlist\", and the skipReason message next to it when present (REQ-23).\n- disabled: show the reason text.\n\nActions:\n- Book: optimistic footer → bookSession. On success show the toast \"You're booked for <name> · <Ddd HH:mm>\" with Undo for 5 s (undoBooking). On a 409 class_full, refetch, and the page shows the full state and the 'Join waitlist' footer (REQ-48). On other 409s show the inline validation message (e.g. the overlap text) and an error toast. On any failure restore the previous state.\n- Join waitlist and Leave waitlist (confirm dialog) show a confirmation toast with no Undo.\n- Cancel booking opens the generated confirm dialog. It shows the 'Late cancellation — this counts as a missed class.' warning when myBooking.lateIfCancelledNow is true. Confirming calls cancelBooking. Escape or dismiss leaves everything unchanged, and focus goes back to the trigger (use the kit dialog's focus trap). A 409 invalid_booking_state shows 'This booking can't be changed any more. Refresh to see its latest status.' and refetches.\n\nBack: if a `back` search param is present, router.push it; otherwise router.back(), falling back to '/'. This keeps the Schedule's day, week, filters and the Bookings tab (REQ-44). When embedded, the onClose prop replaces Back. Call usePromotionNotices().","conventions":["Call the API only through the generated lib/api client after configureLocalApi(); never import lib/booking from components","Do not restyle or rebuild the generated page; pass data and handlers into its existing props, states and copy","Toasts and errors show plain-language messages only (NFR-8)"],"dependsOn":["TASK-3"],"exemplars":["components/screens/s-2/container.tsx","app/classes/[sessionId]/page.tsx"],"fileScope":["components/screens/s-2/container.tsx","components/screens/s-2/use-class-detail.ts"],"id":"TASK-4","plannedLoc":320,"reqs":["REQ-23","REQ-41","REQ-42","REQ-44","REQ-45","REQ-46","REQ-47","REQ-48","REQ-57","REQ-63","REQ-17","REQ-19","REQ-31","REQ-39"],"title":"S-2 Class Detail container: real data, footer actions, cancel dialog, rejections"},{"approach":"use-schedule-state.ts keeps week (current|next), day (YYYY-MM-DD), type[], intensity[] and time[] in search params via router.replace. Day defaults to calendar.today. The previous arrow is disabled on the current week and the next arrow on the next week. Days with sessionCount 0 are dimmed.\n\nLoad getScheduleCalendar and listSessions({date, type, intensity, timeOfDay}). Page states:\n- loading: skeleton cards\n- no sessions on the day at all: 'No classes on this day'\n- filters leave nothing: 'No classes match your filters' plus Clear filters\n- a failed call: the approved error copy with Retry\n\nThe card button comes from actionState.label. Book and Join are optimistic: update the card at once, and keep a per-session in-flight lock so double taps send one request (NFR-7). On success, replace the card with the returned session. Book shows the toast \"You're booked for <name> · <Ddd HH:mm>\" with Undo for 5 s, and Undo calls undoBooking and restores the returned session. Join shows a confirmation toast with no Undo. On a 409 or 500, roll back to the previous card and show the error toast with the server's plain message.\n\nActivating the card body, or the Booked ✓ / Waitlisted / disabled button, opens detail. Below 1024 px (matchMedia), router.push('/classes/'+id+'?back='+encodeURIComponent(current URL)). From 1024 px, set ?session=id and render the S-2 container in the page's side-panel slot with onClose that removes the param. Call usePromotionNotices() on mount (REQ-24).","conventions":["Call the API only through the generated lib/api client after configureLocalApi()","Do not restyle the generated page; feed its props, states and copy","Filter, day and week state live in URL search params so Back restores them"],"dependsOn":["TASK-4"],"exemplars":["components/screens/s-1/container.tsx","app/page.tsx"],"fileScope":["components/screens/s-1/container.tsx","components/screens/s-1/use-schedule-state.ts"],"id":"TASK-5","plannedLoc":360,"reqs":["REQ-1","REQ-2","REQ-7","REQ-24","REQ-25","REQ-33","REQ-34","REQ-35","REQ-36","REQ-37","REQ-38","REQ-39","REQ-40","REQ-41","REQ-42","REQ-43","REQ-58","NFR-2","NFR-7"],"title":"S-1 Schedule container: week/day/filters in URL, cards, optimistic book/join, undo, side panel"},{"approach":"Load getMember, getMyStats and listMyBookings in parallel. Show skeleton rows while loading, and the approved error copy with Retry on failure.\n\nHeader: AR avatar, name, membership. Three stat tiles from the stats response. The tab comes from ?tab=upcoming|past (router.replace).\n\nUpcoming groups use the server's labels. Each row has the booking badge and a Cancel (Booked) or Leave (Waitlisted) action. Disable that action when booking.session.startsAt ≤ now ('Class has started').\n\nEmpty states: Upcoming shows 'No upcoming classes' with Browse schedule → '/'. Past shows 'Your class history will appear here.'.\n\nQuick Cancel opens the generated confirm overlay, with the late warning when lateIfCancelledNow is true. Leave opens the leave overlay. On confirm, update optimistically: move the row to Past with the 'Cancelled'/'Late cancel' badge. Then call cancelBooking or leaveWaitlist, show the confirmation toast (no Undo), and refetch the stats and lists. On failure, restore the row and show the error toast. A 409 invalid_booking_state uses the approved validation copy and refetches.\n\nActivating a row calls router.push('/classes/'+sessionId+'?back='+encodeURIComponent('/bookings?tab='+tab)). Call usePromotionNotices().","conventions":["Call the API only through the generated lib/api client after configureLocalApi()","Do not restyle the generated page; feed its props, overlays and copy","Selected tab lives in the ?tab= search param"],"dependsOn":["TASK-3"],"exemplars":["components/screens/s-3/container.tsx","app/bookings/page.tsx"],"fileScope":["components/screens/s-3/container.tsx"],"id":"TASK-6","plannedLoc":260,"reqs":["REQ-1","REQ-26","REQ-27","REQ-28","REQ-30","REQ-39","REQ-41","REQ-42","REQ-47","REQ-49","REQ-50","REQ-57","REQ-63","REQ-17","REQ-18","REQ-19"],"title":"S-3 My Bookings container: profile, stats, Upcoming/Past tabs, quick cancel/leave"}]}